http: a body sent as bare deflate is read

`Content-Encoding: deflate` means deflate inside a zlib wrapper. Servers
written on .NET, a widely used media server among them, send deflate
with nothing around it under that name. The inflater was set up to find
a gzip or a zlib header, found neither, and every read of the body came
back empty with a warning: a playlist sent that way could not be read.

When the very first bytes of a body fail as a header, the same bytes are
now read again as bare deflate, which is what curl and the browsers do.
A body with a header is read as before.

FFmpeg's connections state no `Accept-Encoding`, so a server that goes
by what it is asked sends them nothing compressed. This is for the one
that compresses anyway, and for a caller that adds the header itself.

--- a/libavformat/http.c	2026-11-14 02:22:14
+++ b/libavformat/http.c	2026-11-14 02:22:14
@@ -1840,7 +1840,7 @@
 static int http_buf_read_compressed(URLContext *h, uint8_t *buf, int size)
 {
     HTTPContext *s = h->priv_data;
-    int ret;
+    int ret, fresh;
 
     if (!s->inflate_buffer) {
         s->inflate_buffer = av_malloc(DECOMPRESS_BUF_SIZE);
@@ -1859,7 +1859,23 @@
     s->inflate_stream.avail_out = size;
     s->inflate_stream.next_out  = buf;
 
+    fresh = s->inflate_stream.total_in == 0;
     ret = inflate(&s->inflate_stream, Z_SYNC_FLUSH);
+    if (ret == Z_DATA_ERROR && fresh) {
+        /* "deflate" means deflate inside a zlib wrapper, and some servers
+         * send it bare all the same. What fails then is the wrapper's
+         * header, in the first two bytes: begin again, and read the same
+         * bytes as deflate with nothing around it. */
+        unsigned available = s->inflate_stream.avail_in +
+                             (unsigned)(s->inflate_stream.next_in - s->inflate_buffer);
+        if (inflateReset2(&s->inflate_stream, -15) == Z_OK) {
+            s->inflate_stream.next_in   = s->inflate_buffer;
+            s->inflate_stream.avail_in  = available;
+            s->inflate_stream.avail_out = size;
+            s->inflate_stream.next_out  = buf;
+            ret = inflate(&s->inflate_stream, Z_SYNC_FLUSH);
+        }
+    }
     if (ret != Z_OK && ret != Z_STREAM_END)
         av_log(h, AV_LOG_WARNING, "inflate return value: %d, %s\n",
                ret, s->inflate_stream.msg);
